      "description": "Segmented filter; the selected tab is a solid ink panel.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-seg\"><button class=\"on\">All <span>24</span></button><button>Passed <span>18</span></button><button>Blocked <span>3</span></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-seg{display:inline-flex;gap:2px;border:1px solid var(--border-2,rgba(16,22,30,.16));border-radius:var(--r,6px);padding:2px;background:var(--surface,#fff)}.ds-seg button{font:650 12.5px 'Overpass Variable',Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif;height:26px;padding:1px 11px 0;border:none;border-radius:var(--r-sm,5px);background:transparent;color:var(--text-2,#464d57);cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}.ds-seg button span{color:var(--text-3,#69717c);font-size:11.5px}.ds-seg button:hover{background:var(--hover,rgba(16,22,30,.045));color:var(--text,#12161b)}.ds-seg button.on{background:var(--ink,#12161b);color:var(--ink-fg,#fff)}.ds-seg button.on span{color:rgba(255,255,255,.65)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status and Severity",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "sev-must-fix",
      "description": "Station-marker status plus severity badges; shape first, colour second.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-row\"><span class=\"ds-status\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8\" r=\"7\" fill=\"var(--ok,#0b7a43)\"/><path d=\"M4.9 8.2 7 10.2 11.1 5.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg><span>Passed</span></span><span class=\"ds-sev must\">Must fix</span><span class=\"ds-sev con\">Consider</span><span class=\"ds-sev min\">Minor</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-row{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;font-family:'Overpass Variable',Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-status{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ok,#0b7a43)}.ds-sev{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:22px;padding:1px 7px 0;border-radius:var(--r-sm,5px);font-size:12px;font-weight:750}.ds-sev.must{background:var(--danger,#cc2a1f);color:var(--on-status,#fff)}.ds-sev.con{color:var(--warn,#b26800);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn,#b26800) 15%,transparent)}.ds-sev.min{color:var(--text-2,#464d57);background:var(--surface-2,#f5f5f7);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border-2,rgba(16,22,30,.16))}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "Flat hairline surface; lifts only on hover when clickable.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-card\"><div class=\"ds-ct\">Full review</div><p>Context seed forked into six lenses, verified, gated.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-card{width:300px;background:var(--surface,#fff);border:1px solid var(--border,rgba(16,22,30,.1));border-radius:var(--r-lg,9px);padding:18px 20px;font:400 13.5px/1.5 'Overpass Variable',Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--text-2,#464d57);transition:border-color .15s,box-shadow .2s;cursor:pointer}.ds-card:hover{border-color:var(--border-3,rgba(16,22,30,.3));box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(16,22,30,.08),0 1px 3px rgba(16,22,30,.06)}.ds-ct{font-weight:750;font-size:15px;color:var(--text,#12161b);margin-bottom:6px}.ds-card p{margin:0}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Block Node",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "block-node",
      "description": "Graph node: round type bullet, label, mono summary, station marker, status footer.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-node\"><div class=\"ds-top\"><span class=\"ds-tile\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"7\"/><path d=\"m21 21-4.3-4.3\"/></svg></span><div class=\"ds-tt\"><div class=\"ds-lbl\">Context · gather facts</div><div class=\"ds-sum\">claude · sonnet</div></div><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8\" r=\"7\" fill=\"var(--ok,#0b7a43)\"/><path d=\"M4.9 8.2 7 10.2 11.1 5.9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></svg></div><div class=\"ds-st\"><b>Done</b> 42s</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-node{width:232px;background:var(--surface,#fff);border:1.5px solid var(--border-2,rgba(16,22,30,.16));border-radius:var(--r-lg,9px);box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(16,22,30,.06);font:12.5px 'Overpass Variable',Overpass,system-ui,sans-serif;transition:border-color .2s}.ds-node:hover{border-color:var(--border-3,rgba(16,22,30,.3))}.ds-top{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:10px 11px 9px}.ds-tile{width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--c-context,#1b3f99);flex-shrink:0}.ds-tt{flex:1;min-width:0}.ds-lbl{font-weight:750;font-size:13px;color:var(--text,#12161b);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}.ds-sum{font:11px 'Overpass Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--text-3,#69717c)}.ds-st{font-size:11.5px;padding:6px 11px 5px;border-top:1px solid var(--border,rgba(16,22,30,.1));color:var(--text-3,#69717c)}.ds-st b{color:var(--ok,#0b7a43);font-weight:750}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Instrument",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Quiet Instrument\"**\n\nPuRR is one developer's review instrument, set in the category-standard idiom of a Linear-calibre tool shell and played straight. The shell is monochrome: a neutral grey ground, a sidebar one step darker, white (or graphite) surfaces, hairline borders and solid-ink primary actions. Nothing in the chrome is coloured. When colour appears, it carries meaning, either a state (passed, blocked, failed, running, plus the must-fix / consider / minor severities) or one of the nine flow block types.\n\nDensity is compact and desktop-first: 13.5px body, 30px controls and tight 6–9px corners, so a run's status reads at a glance beside a terminal and an editor. The signature is the flow drawn as a route. Block types are solid round bullets in fixed line colours, graph edges are curves in the source block's colour, and every flow card carries a small route diagram. Motion only ever reports state, like a running pulse or an animated live edge.\n\nThis world was the user's own choice, made after they rejected two directions. One was the first pass's purple→teal gradient accent (\"very common for AI code\"). The other was a transit-map \"signage rail\". Anything that reads as a generic AI SaaS dashboard is wrong.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Monochrome neutral shell. Ink primary buttons, neutral focus rings and neutral selection.",
      "Colour is reserved for state and for the nine block types.",
      "Status is coded by shape first (station markers) and by colour second.",
      "Flat hairline-bordered surfaces. Shadows appear only on floating layers and graph nodes.",
      "Light tokens at `:root`, with a full dark set under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`.",
      "Overpass for UI, Overpass Mono for code, with tabular numerals throughout."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colour-Is-Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Every hue on screen is either a state or a block type. Chrome, focus, selection, links and primary actions stay neutral ink. A colour that means nothing is a defect.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Accent Rule",
        "body": "There is no brand accent colour. Links are ink and are underlined inside running text. They are never tinted.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint, Not Fill Rule",
        "body": "State backgrounds are `color-mix` tints of the state colour (7–15%) over the surface. The only solid state fills are the must-fix severity, the failed and passed station-marker discs, and the solid danger button.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "The body sets `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`, so counts, durations and meters never jitter as they update live.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Borrowed Dot Rule",
        "body": "Overpass draws the middle dot off-centre. A `purr-dot` face maps U+00B7 to Helvetica/Arial so names like \"Lens · Security\" sit level. Keep it at the head of the sans stack.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-At-Rest Rule",
        "body": "Cards, tables and panels never carry a shadow at rest. A shadow means the thing floats, is being hovered, or is selected.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every colour tied to a state or a block type; primary actions use ink (`ink`).",
      "**Do** code status by shape first with station markers, then by colour.",
      "**Do** draw graph edges as curves in the source block's colour, and show a block type only as its round bullet.",
      "**Do** keep surfaces flat with hairline borders; reserve shadows for nodes, hover lift, modals and toasts.",
      "**Do** ship every new token in both the `:root` light set and the `prefers-color-scheme: dark` set.",
      "**Do** honour `prefers-reduced-motion`: animations and transitions collapse, and the running pulse, spinner and live edge stop.",
      "**Do** keep `.desktop` traffic-light clearance and drag regions on any new header-level bar, with `no-drag` on its controls.",
      "**Do** keep loudness for real blocks and must-fixes; everything else stays calm grey."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** introduce a brand accent colour, a purple→teal gradient, or anything that reads as a generic AI SaaS dashboard.",
      "**Don't** bring back the transit-map \"signage rail\" direction the user rejected.",
      "**Don't** colour focus rings, selection, links or nav state.",
      "**Don't** use solid state fills where a 7–15% tint will do; must-fix is the one loud badge.",
      "**Don't** use motion as decoration. It reports running, live or arriving state only.",
      "**Don't** set uppercase letter-spaced labels or eyebrow text above titles."
    ]
  }
}
